        <h1>COMMENTS</h1>
		<h3>Overall Structure</h3>
		<p>My website consists of four pages respectively are "index.html"/"past.html"/"future.html"/"comments.html". Users can click on the four options in the navigation bar or the four options at the footer to switch to the corresponding page.</p>
		<h3>Internal Structure </h3>
		<p>In terms of structure, each page remains consistent. The navigation bar is located at the top of the page, followed by the title of this page, then the main content. At the bottom of each page, there is a footer.</p>
		<h3>Styles Used</h3>
		<p>This website uses a range of CSS styles to control layout, text, images and overall appearance. <b>Flexbox</b> is used in the navigation bar to arrange links horizontally and centre them on the page. <b>Text styles</b> are applied to headings and paragraphs, including font size, colour and alignment.  <b>Background colours and borders </b> used to separate different sections of the page, such as content areas and the footer. 
<b>Rounded corners </b> applied to elements like content boxes and images to improve visual appearance. 
<b>Tables </b> styled with borders and alternating row colours to improve readability. </p>
         <p>Below is a simple table that illustrates some of the styles</p>
            <table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Selector</th>
