		<h3>Graphic Design Aspects</h3>
		<p>For this website, I adopted a simple and gray-white style to enhance the visual appeal. Regarding the layout of the navigation bar, I referred to some popular web page designs online and finally decided to place four buttons at the top to switch pages. Below the buttons, the name of the current page is displayed. I also widened the spacing between the letters of the name to make it more aesthetically pleasing. For the footer, I used a relatively standard design and kept the color consistent with the website.</p>
		<h3>About "alt" tag</h3>
		<p>The alt attribute is used in all images on this website to provide a text description of the image content. 
This ensures that users who cannot see the images can still understand what the image represents.</p>
        <div class="newsitem"> img src="picture2.jpg" alt="picture of myself" </div>
        <h3>About the website works without css</h3>
		<P>When the website lacks CSS, it can still display text and images normally, but it will lack page layout, color adjustments, and image adjustments. However, the functionality of the page will not be affected.</P>
        	
